abstract: "Exact optimum of the Fisher information over all fixed Gaussian measurements (including ancilla-assisted) on m copies of a pure single-mode Gaussian model; attained by concentrating the mean into one bright output and homodyne detection. Also: exact optimum under a seed-squeezing cap, exact shortfall from the quantum Fisher information, and a criterion for strict collective advantage. Unrefereed candidate; internal AI-assisted review only. Text CC0-1.0; code MIT."
